From 9bfbef7c57699aecdbd0cd4f74b9243997c88863 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:01:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 0049 the image did not contain the tools the instructions
 name (5887 passed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The book deployed to Fly — machine 08054eda399e48, Frankfurt, image built
and pushed — and the next command in the printed instructions was

    flyctl ssh console --app carry-book -C "python3 tools/drill.py"

which would have failed with NO SUCH FILE. The Dockerfile copies exactly two
tools, connector_check.py and session_tail.py, and deploy.sh tells the
operator to run four.

test_dockerfile.py checks the import closure of main.py, so it guarantees
the BOT can start. Nobody ever asked whether the TOOLS a human is told to
run are shipped. Different question, same consequence: an instruction that
cannot be followed, discovered at the one moment it matters.

test_image_ships_the_tools.py parses deploy.sh for every tools/*.py it
names — including inside the block it prints at the end — and requires each
one in the image, plus the import closure of each shipped tool. The inverse
is deliberately NOT asserted: the image may hold a tool the script never
mentions; what it may not do is promise one it does not have. COPY tools/ is
still refused.

D36 — fly launch REWRITES fly.toml. It printed "Wrote config file fly.toml"
on the very run that deployed, so the check in step 2 validated a document
that no longer existed. A launch that dropped `strategy = immediate` or
added an [http_service] with auto_stop would have given a machine that can
run two books, or be stopped while holding a hedge. The same check runs
again after launch now, and a failure exits 1 rather than warning.

F12 — THE KEY IS NOT IP-PINNED, and that is recorded rather than quietly
skipped. `fly ips allocate-egress` is disabled for trial organisations until
a card is on file, so there is no static egress address to pin to. Accepted
for BYBIT_VENUE=demo ONLY: no real money, no withdrawal rights, simulated
matching, a key useless anywhere but the demo venue. NOT accepted for
mainnet — deploy.sh refuses mainnet outright and the pinning rule has not
moved. The script now says exactly that instead of printing a shrug.

And the PATH note: flyctl installs into ~/.fly/bin and updates .bashrc,
which the shell that ran the installer has not re-read, so every command in
the printed instructions failed with "command not found". The script says so
when it detects it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MVNUn9gHXLEqzyyoU2LjND
